# Receipt Bot verifier (rb.py v18)

Save the code below exactly as `~/receipt-bot/rb.py` and run `python3 ~/receipt-bot/rb.py setup --tz {owner IANA zone}` (add `--job {job id}` once known). `SELFTEST OK` is the gate. SHA-256 `992810cefd961496b599b1632ff4691fc759cc99f4890223eec7f5e5fcaffb1e`; if it differs but selftest passes, tell the owner once. Python 3.9+ standard library only; it reads zambo.dev with plain web requests.

Commands: `setup` (zone, job, selftest, sync), `nightly` (the whole nightly routine), `intake` (any receipt, workflow or handover link or id), `commit`, `week`, `sync`, `hostatus`, `since`; `fetch`, `sweep`, `doctor`, `digest` are the nightly steps run on their own.

Verdicts: OK; REJECT (reason); WITHHELD (never verified, proof or shared); RETRY (pending, or a shape change); DUPLICATE, PREVIOUSLY_*; HOUSEKEEPING (not filed); NEED_FULL_ID; NO_RECEIPT_FOUND. OK: the verify API agrees, your SHA-256 of `canonical_bytes` equals `output_hash`, tool and provenance match. Workflow and handover links get the Merkle root rebuilt under their declared merkle_version (receipt-id-v0 or seq-output-v1), every step and source checked, and `client_decision` plus the not checked, not run and not proven lists.

Nightly output: QUIET or NO_JOB (send nothing; QUIET commits itself), NETWORK with the exact call to make (exit 5), READ_FAILED line (exit 3, nothing marked), or the digest to send followed by `rb.py commit`. `since` on the Zambo read is inclusive, so rb.py reads from 1 ms after the watermark and skips anything at or before it; pages are named by UTC date and swept from the saved list.

Never checked: issuer identity, the outside timestamp anchor, a final output hash, truncation, whether the goal succeeded, bytes behind redacted handover copies. Never edit verdict or parsing logic to pass; if all fails after a zambo.dev change, file nothing and tell the owner.

```python
"""Zambo Receipt Bot verifier v18 (AER-1 -26). Python 3.9+ stdlib. Verified = bytes unchanged since Zambo saved them, not that the answer is right.
rb.py setup [--tz ZONE] [--job ID] | nightly [--paste FILE] | intake [--ws W --bot B --what T --tier b|c] TEXT | workflow [--parent WID] TEXT | hostatus TEXT
rb.py week [--days N] | sync [--force] | fetch [--job ID] [--paste FILE] | sweep|doctor [PAGE...] | digest | commit | since [--set TS] | selftest
